# SkyLedger rules

- TypeScript on Node 22, ESM, run with `tsx`. No build step. Keep runtime dependencies at zero beyond `tsx`.
- Numbers (distances, unit conversions, ratios) come from SQL or code, never from a model reply.
- Every agent step logs through `Tracer.log` with agent_name, action, input_summary, output_summary, target_agent, confidence, retry_count, status.
- `SAMPLE_MODE=true` must keep working with no network and no credentials. Every live call (Zetaris, Meterless) needs a logged fallback.
- Meterless calls go only through `app/adapters/meterless.ts` (headers `meterless-app`, `meterless-scope: user`; never log the token).
- Zetaris calls go only through `app/adapters/zetaris.ts`, one SQL statement per call.
- `vendor/` is third-party (Meterless, Apache-2.0): do not edit it.
- Guarded language: "inconsistent with available data"; never fraud, violation or intent.
- Never put secrets in code, logs or commits. `.env` is filled by the user.
